{"id":"S0231","name":"Invoke-PSImage","description":"Invoke-PSImage takes a PowerShell script and embeds the bytes of the script into the pixels of a PNG image. It generates a one liner for executing either from a file of from the web. Example of usage is embedding the PowerShell code from the Invoke-Mimikatz module and embed it into an image file. By calling the image file from a macro for example, the macro will download the picture and execute the PowerShell code, which in this case will dump the passwords.","kind":"attack_tool","upstream_type":"tool","stix_id":"tool--b52d6583-14a2-4ddc-8527-87fd2142558f","source_modified":"2025-04-16T20:38:55.222Z","aliases":["Invoke-PSImage"],"platforms":[],"source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0231","source_domains":["enterprise"],"classification_note":"Included because the active pinned ATT&CK object has type tool. This is an upstream classification, not an assurance of benignness or a recommendation to run it.","page":"tools/S0231/","reviewed_on":"2026-09-27","guides":[],"guide_currentness":"Historical guides retain publication dates. Commands and product availability have not been revalidated.","techniques":[{"key":"enterprise/T1027.003","id":"T1027.003","name":"Steganography","domain":"enterprise","page":"techniques/enterprise/T1027.003/","environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--c09c2f08-3bda-4af7-9578-01fa1c7fba2c","description":"Invoke-PSImage can be used to embed a PowerShell script within the pixels of a PNG file.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0231","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Adams, B. (2017, December 17). Invoke-PSImage. Retrieved April 10, 2018.","url":"https://github.com/peewpw/Invoke-PSImage"}]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","tag":"File Access","page":"telemetry